This is not the installed Grok 1.0.52 executable or a stable SDK.
Upstream first-party code is Apache-2.0. Preserve upstream LICENSE and
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES in prepared source distributions.
The selected-file contract and instruction are shared with the existing
Freight Chain native Codex package, without using Codex for inference.

Preliminary tests never authorize production authentication or inference.

Private source adaptations add a cached-only/read-only auth initializer and
resolver mode, explicit missing-credential refusal, bounded sampler streams,
a fixed native routing facade, snapshot-only auth policy parsing and a
forced-MDM refusal check. Every adapted upstream file carries a modification
notice. Automatic login/refresh and unsupported managed policy are not enabled.

The review package's routing module is a mechanically projected copy of the
pinned native inject_url_derived_headers function, with only module references
relocated to the existing lightweight native HTTP and shell-base crates.
Preparation compares the complete projection against the pinned upstream body.
The full agent shell/tool/UI crate is not linked into the review broker.
